[I] nanobind: tiny and efficient C++/Python bindings

[T] nanobind is a small binding library that exposes C++ types in Python and
[T] vice versa, reminiscent of Boost.Python and pybind11. Compared to
[T] pybind11 it achieves considerably smaller binaries, faster compile times
[T] and lower runtime overhead.

[U] https://github.com/wjakob/nanobind

[A] wjakob
[M] andrei32 <andrei32.t2@gmail.com>

[C] extra/tool
[F] CROSS OBJDIR

[L] BSD
[V] 3.1.0

[D] 18f4810f5c867fb7f37937eac9ba8ecb82313aab7dd842662da3b56c nanobind-3.1.0.tar.gz https://github.com/wjakob/nanobind/archive/v3.1.0/

var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DNB_USE_SUBMODULE_DEPS=OFF
var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DNB_TEST=OFF

# the Python package and its CMake config belong into site-packages, not the prefix top level
pysitedir=$libdir/python$(pkgprefix ver python | sed 's/\.[0-9]*$//')/site-packages
var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DNB_INSTALL_DATADIR=$pysitedir/nanobind

# CMake searches $libdir/cmake/<name>, link the config there
hook_add postmake 5 'mkdir -p $root$libdir/cmake; ln -sfn ../${pysitedir#$libdir/}/nanobind/cmake $root$libdir/cmake/nanobind'
